* Allow input buttons to be constant values.
  Click the button pops a dialog that lets one type a value.
  The value is then shown 'floating' to the left of the button
  in place of an input connection.

* WHAT OUR WIDGETS SHOULD HANDLE
  > Handle graphic representations of boxes and their buttons
  > Handle connect lines between buttons
  > Simple button-to-button access (ie. one button can get you
    to other button connected to it)
  > Adding/removing buttons
  > zooming/scaling/scrolling desk
  > automatic tooltips

* WHAT OUR WIDGETS SHOULD *NOT* HANDLE
  > Popup menus over buttons/boxes (let user handle right click events)
  > Variable type checking (we provide events/callback app can react to)
  > Code gen (app can walk our tree via the buttons)
  > Load/Save boxes (app can determine xywh, titles, own data, etc)

* USER SHOULD BE ABLE TO DERIVE CLASS FROM OpButton
  ..so that they can handle own data on create/destroy,
  and handle() events (connect attempts, dragover, clicks, codegen..)

* USER CAN HANDLE CODEGEN STUFF WITH THEIR OWN CODE

* When box 'selected', OpBox should draw a rectangle around perimiter
  (similar to how connection lines draw between boxes in context of desk)

* When creating buttons, box handles their xywh positioning automatically.

* App can enlarge/shrink OpBox, which should keep buttons same size
  allowing center to expand, with image staying 'centered'.

* Connections are managed in several ways:

	> The OpDesk maintains a list of all button-to-button connections
	  in its connects[] vector array. This is useful to quickly walk
	  all the interconnections for saving layouts, and drawing connection
	  lines.

	> Each OpButton keeps track of the OpButton(s) it's connected to
	  in the connected_to[] vector array.


* EXAMPLE:
                                                                    Fl_Group (OpBox)
                                                                   /
   _________________                   ---------------------------/
   |    Add_24     |                  |                           |
   -----------------                  |  ---                 ---  |
   | A |       |   |                  | |   |               |   | |
   |---|       |Out|                  | |   |               |   | |
   | B |       |   |                  |  ---\                ---\ |
   -----------------                  |      \                   \|
                                       -------\-------------------\
                                               \___________________\__ Fl_Button (OpButton)
   class MyAddBox : public OpBox {
       OpInputButton *a;
       OpInputButton *b;
       OpOutputButton *out;
       MyAddBox(X,Y,W,H,T,IMG) : OpBox(X,Y,W,H,T,IMG) {
            // create codegen data, buttons, tooltips, add self to desk..
	   tooltip("This is an 'add' box");		// [OPTIONAL] shows up over top of widget
	   a = new OpInputButton("A", this);		// create 'a' input button, add to self
	   b = new OpInputButton("B", this);		// create 'b' input button, add to self
	   out = new OpOutputButton("out", this);
       }
       // HANDLE EVENTS TO BOX
       int handle(int e) {
         case FL_PUSH, FL_RELEASE:		// handle clicks on box
	    break;
	 case FL_ENTER/DRAG/LEAVE/FOCUS:	// mouse entered/left box (return 0 if not interested)
	    break;
       }
    };
    class MyInputButton : public OpInputButton {
	MyInputButton(T) {
	    // associate custom codegen data, varname
	}
        // HANDLE EVENTS TO *BUTTON*
        int handle(int e) {
	    case FL_PUSH, FL_RELEASE:		// handle clicks on box
	        break;
	    case FL_ENTER/DRAG/LEAVE/FOCUS:	// handle someone about to drop/giving up a connection
	        // do tests here to see if incoming connection from 'otherbut' ok
	        break;
	}
        // HANDLE 'CONNECTION EVENTS' TO BUTTON
	int ConnectEvent(int e) {
            case OP_CONNECT_INBOUND:		// someone about to drop a connection on us
            case OP_CONNECT_OUTBOUND:		// someone giving up on a connection to us
	        // IN: can gray out button to indicate rejection
	        // OUT: can un-gray button to restore box to normal
            case OP_CONNECT:			// someone made connection to us
	        // Can accept (return(1)) or reject (return(0);)
	        break;
	}
    };


